Change Purpose

This change is being implemented to remediate Idira Security Bulletin CA26-47, a High Severity (CVSS 8.7) vulnerability affecting the Database Credentials Management Framework (DCMF) version 22.2.0 and earlier. According to the bulletin, the vulnerability may result in the disclosure of sensitive data, potentially leading to unauthorized system access. There is no available workaround or temporary mitigation; therefore, upgrading to the latest supported version is the required remediation. The change aligns with Alliant's Privileged Access Management standards, which require centralized and secure management of privileged credentials.

Business Benefits and Intended Results
Remediate a High Severity security vulnerability identified in Idira Security Bulletin CA26-47.
Reduce the risk of sensitive credential exposure and unauthorized access to critical systems.
Maintain compliance with Alliant's Identity and Access Management and Privileged Access Management security standards.
Ensure continued supportability and alignment with vendor-recommended software versions.
Strengthen the security posture of the Idira/CyberArk platform by implementing the vendor-provided fix.
Improve protection of privileged and application credentials managed through the Database Credentials Management Framework.
High-Level Implementation Steps
Pre-Implementation
Review Idira Security Bulletin CA26-47 and vendor remediation guidance.
Validate current Database Credentials Management Framework version installed on impacted CPM servers.
Download the latest supported DCMF package from the Idira Marketplace.
Confirm successful backup/snapshot of impacted CPM components and configuration files.
Notify impacted stakeholders and application owners.
Implementation
Place impacted CPM services into maintenance/change window.
Install/upgrade the Database Credentials Management Framework to the latest vendor-supported version.
Apply any required configuration updates provided by Idira.
Restart affected CPM services if required.
Verify successful installation and component health.
Validation
Execute credential verification and password rotation tests against representative database accounts.
Review CPM, plugin, and framework logs for errors.
Confirm successful password management operations.
Validate no impact to existing database credential rotations, reconciliations, or privileged access workflows.
Obtain stakeholder approval and close the change.
Backout Plan

If issues are encountered:

Stop affected services.
Restore the previous Database Credentials Management Framework version from backup/snapshot.
Restart CPM services.
Validate password management functionality has returned to its pre-change state.
Escalate to Idira Support if required.
Estimated Change Duration

Single-day implementation (less than 24 hours)

Day 1
Backup and pre-validation.
Upgrade Database Credentials Management Framework.
Service restart and validation testing.
Post-implementation monitoring and change closure.
Expected Outcome

The Database Credentials Management Framework will be upgraded to the latest supported release, fully remediating the vulnerability identified in Idira Security Bulletin CA26-47, while maintaining secure and uninterrupted credential management operations across the Idira/CyberArk environment.
